{
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "autoloader-generic",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [],
      "lines": [
        "The app ships no composer/autoload.php, so the server registers its generic loader for lib/ and looks every class up in the file system.",
        "  A composer/composer.json with config.vendor-dir \".\", config.optimize-autoloader true, a config.autoloader-suffix and autoload.psr-4 {\"OCA\\\\QuickBook\\\\\": \"../lib/\"} makes composer dump-autoload write composer/autoload.php with a class map; the code of the app does not change."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ocp-deprecated",
      "level": "info",
      "places": [
        "lib/Service/BookingFlowService.php:103 OCP\\Mail\\IMailer::validateMailAddress(): deprecated since Nextcloud 32; use IEmailValidator::isValid() instead"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "1 use in 1 file of the public API that is deprecated in Nextcloud 32 to 36. The text of the tag names the replacement where it has one.",
        "  lib/Service/BookingFlowService.php:103 OCP\\Mail\\IMailer::validateMailAddress(): deprecated since Nextcloud 32; use IEmailValidator::isValid() instead"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "job-time-sensitivity",
      "level": "info",
      "places": [
        "lib/BackgroundJob/HealthCheckJob.php OCA\\QuickBook\\BackgroundJob\\HealthCheckJob"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "1 timed job does not say whether it is time sensitive. A job that sets TIME_INSENSITIVE with setTimeSensitivity() is moved to the maintenance window of the server; whether a job is heavy enough for that only its maintainer knows.",
        "  lib/BackgroundJob/HealthCheckJob.php OCA\\QuickBook\\BackgroundJob\\HealthCheckJob"
      ]
    },
